                <pb facs="0543" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg473"/>

                <head>No. 259.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 31,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Hoppin telegraphed to Mr. Frelinghuysen that O’Donnell says he never enlisted
                    in the Army; was only a teamster. Police reports wrong in this and other
                    matters. Mr. Hoppin referred to his dispatch of the 23d October, and added that
                    he had made unsuccessful attempts to ascertain the place and date of the
                    naturalization of O’Donnell’s father, and fears that he cannot obtain further
                    information from the prisoner or solicitor.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
